drm/asahi: report the DRM driver as "asahi" 0.0.0, as upstream Asahi Linux does

Aurora 7.3 (ce3c5d3) names the driver "aurora" with major 1. Stock Mesa (asahi gallium and
the kmsro loader for the "apple" display node) only knows "asahi", so compositors fall back to
software rendering and wlroots refuses to start. The UAPI itself only gained ioctls and
feature bits since 7.2.11, which reported "asahi" 0.0.0.

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/driver.rs
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/driver.rs
@@ -92,10 +92,10 @@
 /// accepts without probing. The patch level marks fixes userspace may need to
 /// detect.
 const INFO: drm::driver::DriverInfo = drm::driver::DriverInfo {
-    major: 1,
+    major: 0,
     minor: 0,
     patchlevel: 0,
-    name: c"aurora",
+    name: c"asahi",
     desc: c"Aurora GPU for Apple AGX",
 };
 
